  "roads": {},
  "notes": "Zone stays suburb. Banepa mixes modern RCC with an older brick bazaar, so about seven in ten buildings of 20 to 250 m2 within 35 m of the old trade lanes (Bhont Marg, Wasinkhyo, Japali, Kwon Lal, Wasinkhyah Bahi, Jyatan Lal) are styled as Newari brick; the rest follow the suburb mix at three storeys. 7 footprints under 8 m2 are removed as slivers, and 6 more that lie more than half under a road ribbon are removed. Footprints under 20 m2 are one storey and under 35 m2 two storeys, since they are sheds and lean-tos. Worship buildings are styled by id as brick temples (small shrines get pitched one-storey roofs); greenhouses, garages and workshops are one-storey tin sheds."
